      en: "The Yeywa Hydropower Plant on the Myitnge River in the Mandalay Region is Myanmar's largest power generation facility. Boasting an installed capacity of 790 megawatts, the plant provides a significant portion of the electricity available in the national grid and is essential for the energy security of Mandalay and Central Myanmar. The facility features a 134-meter-high Roller-Compacted Concrete (RCC) dam, which was one of the largest of its kind in the world upon its completion in 2010. The project was realized with international technological cooperation and represents a milestone in the country's infrastructure development. Beyond power generation, the reservoir assists in water regulation, though its ecological impact on the river system remains a topic of environmental discussion. Yeywa continues to be a central pillar in Myanmar's strategy to harness its vast hydropower potential to meet increasing industrial and domestic energy demands.",
      es: "La central hidroeléctrica de Yeywa, en el río Myitnge, región de Mandalay, es la tercera mayor de Myanmar con una potencia instalada de 790 MW. Entró en funcionamiento en 2009 y desempeña un papel central en el suministro eléctrico nacional, especialmente para la zona seca. La presa tiene 135 m de altura y 900 m de longitud. El proyecto fue ejecutado por la Myanmar Electric Power Enterprise y empresas chinas. Suministra electricidad a cerca del 10% del país y reduce la dependencia de las centrales de gas.",
